# language: en

Feature: UnSubscribe

    Scenario Outline: The unsubscribe request for a signal that is currently subscribed has been successfully processed
        Given a signal at <path> is set to <value_0> of datatype <datatype>
        And attempts to subscribe the signal at <path> of datatype <datatype> is succeeded
        Then attempts to unsubscribe the signal at <path> of datatype <datatype> is succeeded

    Examples:
        | path                                                     | datatype  | value_0     |
        | Vehicle.Body.Hood.IsLocked | bool | false |
        | Vehicle.Body.Hood.IsOpen | bool | false |
        | Vehicle.Body.Hood.Position | uint8 | 50 |
        | Vehicle.Body.Horn.IsActive | bool | false |
        | Vehicle.Body.IsAutoPowerOptimize | bool | false |
        | Vehicle.Body.Lights.Backup.IsDefect | bool | false |
        | Vehicle.Body.Lights.Backup.IsOn | bool | false |
        | Vehicle.Body.Lights.Beam.High.IsDefect | bool | false |
        | Vehicle.Body.Lights.Beam.High.IsOn | bool | false |
        | Vehicle.Body.Lights.Beam.Low.IsDefect | bool | false |
        | Vehicle.Body.Lights.Beam.Low.IsOn | bool | false |
        | Vehicle.Body.Lights.Brake.IsActive | string | ACTIVE |
        | Vehicle.Body.Lights.Brake.IsDefect | bool | false |
        | Vehicle.Body.Lights.DirectionIndicator.Left.IsDefect | bool | false |
